To center the text vertically on an image using HTML and CSS, you can use flexbox or position absolute/relative technique.

Method 1: Using Flexbox
HTML:
```html
<div class="container">
  <img src="image.jpg" alt="image">
  <div class="text">The text you want to center</div>
</div>
```
CSS:
```css
.container {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  flex-direction: column;
  height: 100vh;
}

.text {
  text-align: center;
}
```

Method 2: Using absolute/relative positioning
HTML:
```html
<div class="container">
  <img src="image.jpg" alt="image">
  <div class="text">The text you want to center</div>
</div>
```
CSS:
```css
.container {
  position: relative;
}

.text {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
  text-align: center;
}
```

Both methods share the same HTML structure, where the image and text are wrapped inside a container element. The container element is styled with CSS to ensure its height covers the entire viewport (`height: 100vh`), and the `display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;` is used to center the content vertically and horizontally using flexbox method. 

In the second method, the container element is relatively positioned and the text element is absolutely positioned. The `top: 50%; left: 50%;` along with `transform: translate(-50%, -50%);` helps center the text vertically and horizontally within the container.

I apologize for the misunderstanding. If you want to vertically center the text over the image, you can use absolute positioning.

HTML:
```html
<div class="container">
  <img src="image.jpg" alt="image">
  <div class="text">The text you want to center</div>
</div>
```
CSS:
```css
.container {
  position: relative;
}

.text {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
  text-align: center;
}
```

In this method, the `.container` class is relatively positioned, and the `.text` class is absolutely positioned within it. The `top: 50%` and `left: 50%` properties position the text element at the center of the container. The `transform: translate(-50%, -50%)` property helps to precisely center the text both vertically and horizontally. The `text-align: center` property centers the text horizontally within the `.text` element.

Please keep in mind that this method assumes the container and image have a defined height. If the container's height is not explicitly set, it will collapse, and the text will not be centered properly.

